<p><b>Xedoc's Bio:</b>
<table border=1 width=400>
  <tr><td>
  <html>
<body>Like all young Teir'Dal children Xedoc grew up in what could be called a "typical" household. His father was a proud devotee to their Immortal Lord Innoruuk as he carried about as his duties as one of the noble city guards. His mother was a priestess within the Hall of Hate. He was brought up using the sword and learned to show his Hate in devotion to his god at an early age. </body>
<p>
<body>One dark morning Xedoc was playing "Dragoons and Paladins" with his fellow children in the Neriak Commons. As they jousted and feinted playfully something caught their eye. One of the Elder Sorcerors happened to have just returned from a long journey into the the deep deserts of Ro. He was demonstrating to one of his fellow Wizards the sheer raw power of Solusek Ro one a halpless wood elf slave fresh from the Crushbone Castle. As the two Wizards conversed about the wonderous powers of the Lord of Flame, Xedoc stared in awa totally captivated by the marvelous flickering flamers consuming the wood elf. It was this pivotal moment that sealed young Xedoc's future.</body>
<p>
<body>Throughout his youth he studied long into the nights about the applications and teachings of the great Wizards from the Neriak Library and Sorcerors Guild. During the day however he mentioned none of this, his father worked him hard and wanted a noble and great future for his son. Like all proud fathers he wanted Xedoc to succede him and become one of the most respected Shadow Knights. This unfortunatly was contrary to what Xedoc wanted, but to breath word of such a dream would bring his fathers wrath and hate. Something Xedoc was quick to avoide. The more nights Xedoc spent awake studying old tomes and ancient scrolls the more it fascinated him. Soon he truly believed the powers of the flame and Solusek Ro outmatched the simple Hate Innoruuk's followers preached. This belief would bring conflict to Xedoc sooner than he could imagine.</body>
<p>
<body>One his 18th birthday, a time of much Hate and celebration, Xedoc announced to his family he had been accepted to work as an Acoloyte at the Sorcerors Guild. His rather was devistated and crushed. His hopes and dreams for his son fell like a human to a well placed blow form a sword. It took only a few moments for this feeling to subside and he was consumed with rage. A long and heated argument ensured. Xedoc tried to convince his father that the powers of Ice and Flame were more mighty than Hate any day, however he was unmoved. His father, angry and intolerant warned his son he preached blasphemy to defy the teachings of Innoruu, but Xedoc countered saying he was ignorant and close minded. The war of words lasted several hours, neither giving in. When it finally ended Xedoc was banished from his fathers household and Xedoc vowed never to reutn.</body>
<p>
<body>And so Xedoc set out to the Neriak Commons to learn as much as he could and make a name for himself as one of the greatest Wizards of the Teir'Dal.</body>
